IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cbr-nouns`
IMPORT `cbr-reg2-couples`

-- TESTS OF REGULATION 2(2) AND (3) (src:21-31). Expected values are written from the
-- text. "Elder" is the child born earlier; the text does not say what two children
-- born on the same day are (fork F3), so that case is asserted as NOTHING.

§ `Tests of regulation 2(2) and (3)`

-- A claimant, built from the facts the paragraphs read, in the order of the record:
-- voluntary organisation; living with spouse or civil partner; living with another as
-- spouse or civil partner; (3)(a) party married to more than one person; (3)(b)
-- ceremony under the law of a country which permits polygamy; residing with other
-- members of that marriage.
GIVEN voluntary IS A BOOLEAN
      spouse IS A BOOLEAN
      partner IS A BOOLEAN
      polya IS A BOOLEAN
      polyb IS A BOOLEAN
      residing IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Claimant at the start of the week`
`a claimant with the facts` voluntary spouse partner polya polyb residing MEANS
    `Claimant at the start of the week` WITH
        `a voluntary organisation` IS voluntary
        `living with the claimant's spouse or civil partner` IS spouse
        `living with another person as the claimant's spouse or civil partner` IS partner
        `during the marriage a party to it is married to more than one person` IS polya
        `the ceremony of the marriage took place under the law of a country which permits polygamy` IS polyb
        `residing with other members of that marriage` IS residing

-- Another person listed in paragraph (2)(a), as the claimant sees them.
GIVEN exists IS A BOOLEAN
      born IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Other persons listed in paragraph (2)(a) at the start of the week`
`another person whose child counts` exists born MEANS
    `Other persons listed in paragraph (2)(a) at the start of the week` WITH
        `child benefit would, but for paragraph (2), be payable at the enhanced rate to one of them for another child or qualifying person` IS exists
        `date of birth of the elder or eldest of those other children` IS born

`a claimant living with a spouse` MEANS `a claimant with the facts` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`a claimant living alone` MEANS `a claimant with the facts` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE

§§ `Regulation 2(3) (src:29-31): a member of a polygamous marriage needs both (a) and (b)`

#ASSERT `a claimant is a member of a polygamous marriage` (`a claimant with the facts` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- (a) only: a party is married to more than one person, but the ceremony was under a law that does not permit polygamy.
#ASSERT NOT (`a claimant is a member of a polygamous marriage` (`a claimant with the facts` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE))
-- (b) only: the ceremony was under a law that permits polygamy, but no party is married to more than one person.
#ASSERT NOT (`a claimant is a member of a polygamous marriage` (`a claimant with the facts` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`a claimant is a member of a polygamous marriage` (`a claimant with the facts` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE))

§§ `Regulation 2(2)(a) (src:21-25): living with a spouse or civil partner; living with another as spouse or civil partner; a polygamous marriage and residing with the other members`

#ASSERT `paragraph (2)(a) applies to the claimant` (`a claimant with the facts` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `paragraph (2)(a) applies to the claimant` (`a claimant with the facts` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `paragraph (2)(a) applies to the claimant` (`a claimant with the facts` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
-- (iii) needs both parts: a member of a polygamous marriage AND residing with the other members.
#ASSERT NOT (`paragraph (2)(a) applies to the claimant` (`a claimant with the facts` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`paragraph (2)(a) applies to the claimant` (`a claimant with the facts` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE))
#ASSERT NOT (`paragraph (2)(a) applies to the claimant` (`a claimant with the facts` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE))
#ASSERT NOT (`paragraph (2)(a) applies to the claimant` (`a claimant with the facts` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE))
-- Being a voluntary organisation is not a limb of (2)(a).
#ASSERT NOT (`paragraph (2)(a) applies to the claimant` (`a claimant with the facts` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE))

§§ `Regulation 2(2), closing words (src:28): the elder is the child born earlier`

#ASSERT `the claimant's child is the elder of the children referred to in paragraph (2)(b) and (c)` (Date 1 1 2010) (Date 2 1 2010) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the claimant's child is the elder of the children referred to in paragraph (2)(b) and (c)` (Date 2 1 2010) (Date 1 1 2010) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the claimant's child is the elder of the children referred to in paragraph (2)(b) and (c)` (Date 1 1 2010) (Date 1 1 2010) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Months and years, not only days.
#ASSERT `the claimant's child is the elder of the children referred to in paragraph (2)(b) and (c)` (Date 31 12 2009) (Date 1 1 2010) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the claimant's child is the elder of the children referred to in paragraph (2)(b) and (c)` (Date 1 1 2011) (Date 31 12 2010) EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `Regulation 2(2) (src:21-28): the enhanced rate is payable for only the elder or eldest`

-- All three of (a), (b) and (c): the claimant's child, born 1 January 2010, against the other person's child.
-- The claimant's child is the elder: the enhanced rate is kept for it.
#ASSERT `paragraph (2) allows the enhanced rate for the claimant's child` (`a claimant living with a spouse`) (Date 1 1 2010) TRUE (`another person whose child counts` TRUE (Date 1 1 2012)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The claimant's child is the younger: the enhanced rate is payable for only the other child.
#ASSERT `paragraph (2) allows the enhanced rate for the claimant's child` (`a claimant living with a spouse`) (Date 1 1 2012) TRUE (`another person whose child counts` TRUE (Date 1 1 2010)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Born on the same day: the text does not say, so it is not covered.
#ASSERT `paragraph (2) allows the enhanced rate for the claimant's child` (`a claimant living with a spouse`) (Date 1 1 2010) TRUE (`another person whose child counts` TRUE (Date 1 1 2010)) EQUALS NOTHING
-- A civil partner or a cohabitant: same, by (a)(i) and (ii).
#ASSERT `paragraph (2) allows the enhanced rate for the claimant's child` (`a claimant with the facts` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) (Date 1 1 2012) TRUE (`another person whose child counts` TRUE (Date 1 1 2010)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A polygamous household: same, by (a)(iii).
#ASSERT `paragraph (2) allows the enhanced rate for the claimant's child` (`a claimant with the facts` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE) (Date 1 1 2012) TRUE (`another person whose child counts` TRUE (Date 1 1 2010)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (a) fails: the claimant lives alone, so paragraph (2) does not touch the child however old the other person's child is.
#ASSERT `paragraph (2) allows the enhanced rate for the claimant's child` (`a claimant living alone`) (Date 1 1 2012) TRUE (`another person whose child counts` TRUE (Date 1 1 2010)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (a) fails for a polygamous marriage not lived in together.
#ASSERT `paragraph (2) allows the enhanced rate for the claimant's child` (`a claimant with the facts` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE) (Date 1 1 2012) TRUE (`another person whose child counts` TRUE (Date 1 1 2010)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (b) fails: child benefit would not, but for the paragraph, be payable to the claimant at the enhanced rate for this child.
#ASSERT `paragraph (2) allows the enhanced rate for the claimant's child` (`a claimant living with a spouse`) (Date 1 1 2012) FALSE (`another person whose child counts` TRUE (Date 1 1 2010)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (c) fails: it would not be payable at the enhanced rate to one of the other persons.
#ASSERT `paragraph (2) allows the enhanced rate for the claimant's child` (`a claimant living with a spouse`) (Date 1 1 2012) TRUE (`another person whose child counts` FALSE (Date 1 1 2010)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
